{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q418276","formula":"C₁₀H₁₂Cr₂N₂O₇","hill":"C10H12Cr2N2O7","elements":["H","C","N","O","Cr"],"composition":{"C":10.0,"H":12.0,"N":2.0,"O":7.0,"Cr":2.0},"names":{"en":"Cornforth reagent","ru":"Дихромат пиридиния"},"descriptions":{"en":"The Cornforth reagent (pyridinium dichromate or PDC) is a pyridinium salt of dichromate with the chemical formula [C5H5NH]2[Cr2O7]. This compound is named after the Australian-British chemist Sir John Warcup Cornforth, who introduced it in 1962. The Cornforth reagent is a strong oxidizing agent which can convert primary and secondary alcohols to aldehydes and ketones respectively.","ru":"Дихромат пиридиния — соль пиридина и хромовой кислоты, мягкий селективный окислитель, широко применяемый в органическом синтезе, преимущественно для окисления первичных и вторичных спиртов. Данный реагент был предложен Кори и Шмидтом в 1979 году. Потенциальный канцероген."},"fame":15,"pubchemCid":159879,"mass":376.2,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1=CC=NC=C1.C1=CC=NC=C1.O[Cr](=O)(=O)O[Cr](=O)(=O)O","inchikey":"RCBVKBFIWMOMHF-UHFFFAOYSA-L","iupac":"hydroxy-(hydroxy(dioxo)chromio)oxy-dioxochromium;bis(pyridine)","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"159879","atoms":33,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.348,"y":4.298,"z":-2.596,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.482,"y":3.493,"z":-2.607,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.309,"y":2.118,"z":-2.635,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.102,"y":1.512,"z":-2.653,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.019,"y":2.32,"z":-2.642,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.091,"y":3.704,"z":-2.614,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.444,"y":5.38,"z":-2.574,"el":"H"},{"x":-3.476,"y":3.924,"z":-2.593,"el":"H"},{"x":-3.163,"y":1.447,"z":-2.644,"el":"H"},{"x":0.939,"y":1.809,"z":-2.657,"el":"H"},{"x":0.812,"y":4.304,"z":-2.606,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.95,"y":1.123,"z":0.217,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.